{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.numStandardYoungTableaux_le_numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.numStandardYoungTableaux_le_numSYT","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean#L142-L148","doc":"**One half of the bridge**: the 1-indexed count is at most the 0-indexed count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toBraidKnot_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toBraidKnot_injective","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean#L116-L140","doc":"The embedding is **injective**: entries agree on cells (both are `≥ 1`, so the `−1` is\ninvertible there) and vanish off cells, and a tableau is determined by its entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toBraidKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.toBraidKnot","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean#L79-L114","doc":"**The 1-indexed encoding embeds into the 0-indexed one**: subtract one from every entry. All\nsix `QOU.BraidKnot` fields follow from the `Set.BijOn` packaging (`mapsTo_cells` for the bound,\n`injOn_cells` for injectivity) plus the generalized `row_strict` and the underlying\nsemistandard tableau's `col_strict` / `zeros`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_zero_off","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_zero_off","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean#L73-L77","doc":"Off the diagram a 1-indexed entry vanishes (the underlying semistandard tableau's `zeros`,\nin `.entry` form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_le_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.entry_le_card","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean#L68-L71","doc":"On a cell, a 1-indexed entry is at most the cell count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.one_le_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridge.one_le_entry","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SYTEncodingBridge.lean#L63-L66","doc":"On a cell, a 1-indexed entry is positive. ","signatureChunk":0}]}